// Conformance: docs/reference/reference.md §11 with §4.11.
// A struct field carries `@` annotations as a parameter does (§4.11: the
// annotation reflection reads them). They cannot be written on enums,
// globals or other items. Until Nov 23 this file asserted the opposite: the
// list in §11 still named struct fields after §4.11 had allowed them.

struct P {
    @secret x: i64,
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    println(1);
    return 0;
}

//> 1
